# C9 second-channel-set certificate data (adder-family census)

The "second channel set" of `docs/adder-family-2026-08-29.md`: a genuinely
different two-track base-2 disjunction (NOT a complement or single-word swap
of the flagship) on the six constants ln2, ln3, ln6, ln12, ln24, ln72 —
coefficients `(1,0),(0,1),(1,1),(2,1),(3,1),(3,2)` over the tracks
`X = ln2, Y = ln3`, words `00, 001, 11, 00, 00, 010`.

Emitted by `experiments/adder_signed_emit.py secondset` (C1/C1'/C3'
re-verified at emit time); the Lean tables are packed by
`experiments/emit_cert_lean.py` (whose packing is validated to reproduce the
committed C8 tables byte-for-byte).  Ambient 30720 states, 28 live, 6 cycles
(periods 1,2), ρ ≤ 7, ω ≤ 6 (packed 64 states per base-8 chunk, 15×32
two-level).  This is the cheapest certified family in the tower (4× smaller
than the base flagship) — checked here by kernel `decide` against
`zfamPred`, wired via `signed_engine`.
